{
  "id": "COMPOUND:35963 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Picrasin F is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a protein that is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 5,8-Dihydroxy-2-(2-phenylethyl)chromone. These compounds are both implicated in the targeting of NCI-H446, a cell line, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the sialyltransferase enzyme. The shared targeting of this enzyme by different compounds implies that it may play a role in the biological activity of Picrasin F, potentially through a mechanism that involves the modification of sialic acid residues on glycoproteins. The evidence suggests that Picrasin F may act by modulating the activity of this enzyme, which in turn could influence the behavior of NCI-H446 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of sialyltransferase in the drug's mechanism of action and its potential relevance to the biological response of NCI-H446.",
